WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:07.233
Everything around you
is made from a material.

2
00:00:07.453 --> 00:00:11.354
A spoon, a chair, a window.
What is each one made of?

3
00:00:11.854 --> 00:00:16.126
A spoon is an object. An object
is a thing you can point at.

4
00:00:16.346 --> 00:00:19.829
The spoon is made of metal.
Metal is the material.

5
00:00:20.049 --> 00:00:22.882
A chair is an object
too. It is made of wood.

6
00:00:23.102 --> 00:00:26.864
The object is the thing. The
material is what it is made of.

7
00:00:27.084 --> 00:00:32.703
Is the spoon made of spoon? No. Spoon
is what it is. It is made of metal.

8
00:00:32.923 --> 00:00:38.078
One material can make many objects.
Wood makes chairs, pencils and doors.

9
00:00:38.578 --> 00:00:42.200
Wood, metal, plastic, glass,
rock, paper and fabric.

10
00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:45.206
These are seven materials
you see every day.

11
00:00:45.426 --> 00:00:51.417
Outside science, material often means cloth. In
science, it means anything a thing is made of.

12
00:00:51.637 --> 00:00:56.235
Look around the room. Almost everything
you see is made of one of these seven.

13
00:00:56.735 --> 00:01:01.007
Scientists test materials.
Each test tells you a property.

14
00:01:01.227 --> 00:01:06.893
Press it. Is it hard or soft? The
sponge squashes, so it is soft.

15
00:01:07.113 --> 00:01:10.410
Bend it. Does it bend or
break? The sponge bends.

16
00:01:10.630 --> 00:01:14.949
Wet it. Does the water go
through? The sponge soaks it up.

17
00:01:15.169 --> 00:01:18.745
Now test a metal spoon. It is
hard, stiff and waterproof.

18
00:01:18.965 --> 00:01:22.076
Every material has lots
of properties at once.

19
00:01:22.576 --> 00:01:27.406
Squash it, bend it, twist it, stretch
it. Some materials change shape.

20
00:01:27.626 --> 00:01:31.295
Push on clay and it squashes.
Bend it, and it bends.

21
00:01:31.515 --> 00:01:35.973
Pull an elastic band and it
stretches. Twist it round and round.

22
00:01:36.193 --> 00:01:39.583
Push on a stone and nothing
happens. It keeps its shape.

23
00:01:39.803 --> 00:01:42.822
Some materials change
shape, and some do not.

24
00:01:43.322 --> 00:01:49.266
People choose a material because of its
properties. That is science, used every day.

25
00:01:49.486 --> 00:01:52.644
A window is glass because
you can see through it.

26
00:01:52.864 --> 00:01:56.394
A raincoat is plastic
because water runs off it.

27
00:01:56.614 --> 00:02:00.700
A paper raincoat? Paper soaks
up water, so you would get wet.

28
00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:04.264
The right material has the
right properties for the job.

29
00:02:04.764 --> 00:02:08.293
An object is a thing. A
material is what it is made of.

30
00:02:08.513 --> 00:02:12.368
You know seven materials, and
tests find their properties.

31
00:02:12.588 --> 00:02:16.164
Some materials change shape
when you push or pull them.

32
00:02:16.384 --> 00:02:20.888
Choose the right material for the
job. Now go on a material hunt!
